.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt WIFI.CONF 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm wifi.conf
.Nd saved wireless networks
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Pa /etc/novi/wifi.conf
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
holds the networks this machine will join, in
.Nm wpa_supplicant Ns 's
own configuration format \(em it is passed to the supplicant
unmodified.
Manage it with
.Xr novi-wifi 1
rather than by hand.
.Pp
It does not exist until the first network is added.
Mode
.Sy 0600 ,
owned by root.
.Ss Configuration is declared; secrets are not
Only
.Va network.wifi
and
.Va network.wifi.interface
are in
.Xr system.conf 5 .
A passphrase is not, and will not be:
.Xr system.conf 5
is world-readable and this project tells people to commit it to git.
The same rule puts a password hash in
.Pa /etc/shadow
and not in the document.
.Ss The passphrase is on disk in the clear, unavoidably
A WPA3 network block carries
.Va sae_password= ,
which is the plaintext passphrase.
SAE derives from the passphrase rather than from the PBKDF2 pre-shared
key, so there is no one-way transform to store \(em which is why this
file was 0600 and root-only before WPA3 arrived.
.Pp
.Nm novi-wifi add Fl -wpa2-only
is the escape hatch: it writes
.Va psk=
only, no plaintext, and no WPA3.
.Ss WPA2 and WPA3 in one block
A block written by
.Xr novi-wifi 1
carries
.Va key_mgmt=WPA-PSK SAE
and
.Va ieee80211w=1 ,
so it joins whichever the access point offers.
.Va ieee80211w=2
would make every WPA2 access point unjoinable; omitting it entirely
would make every WPA3 one refuse to associate, because SAE requires
protected management frames.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/etc/novi/wifi.conf" -compact
.It Pa /etc/novi/wifi.conf
This file.
.It Pa /run/novi/network.wifi.device
The radio the service resolved, published for readers such as the
panel.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
network={
	ssid="example"
	key_mgmt=WPA-PSK SAE
	ieee80211w=1
	psk=<hex>
	sae_password="the passphrase"
}
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr novi-wifi 1 ,
.Xr system.conf 5
.Sh STANDARDS
RFC 0009, RFC 0021.
.Sh CAVEATS
.Nm wpa_passphrase Ns 's
output ends with
.Ql } ,
so appending to it puts keys at file scope.
.Xr novi-wifi 1
drops the brace, appends, and restores it \(em and refuses rather
than editing blind if the last line is not a brace.
Hand-editing this file is where that goes wrong, and the symptom is
.Nm novi-wifi status
reporting that the supplicant is not running: a message about a
service, produced by a syntax error in a file.
